  FontWeight->Bold],
 " are represented"
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"60d8f826-7d6d-2445-9629-e186b4c3e865"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "all ",
 StyleBox["18 toroidal octave entries",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " per scale are represented"
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"39f1f15e-53df-c846-96c7-7eb8295d111e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "constitutive laws are ",
 StyleBox["per-scale",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["per-octave refinable",
  FontWeight->Bold]
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"c345fd64-ae9e-204f-8d60-c1d62e524b82"],

Cell["\<\
the framework avoids the previous recursion and invalid-option failures\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e740a907-c884-8548-a8d6-486c083e1c6d"],

Cell["\<\
heavy evaluation is possible, but intentionally not auto-triggered for every \
expensive block\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"82f4c010-f957-9a48-ba8d-66b1b2b67021"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The next best step is to refine the ",
 StyleBox["constitutive laws",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " themselves, since that is where the actual physical specificity of each \
scale lives."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8b22bd43-7477-f14e-a913-54ae58abbfc3"]
